      "problem": "Simplify $\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{36}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $a\\ge 0,$ then\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{a}^{2}}=a.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $1$ and $36$ are both perfect squares, where\n\n$$\n1={1}^{2}.\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n36={6}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, to work out $\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{36}},$ we express $\\frac{1}{36}$ as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{36}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{{1}^{2}}{{6}^{2}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{1\\cdot 1}{6\\cdot 6}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
